A||||16||Predator||Need Turbo repair in GA||||11||
Z||000000||Predator||12-18-2000||07:08 PM||||Hey, <P>I drove my Fiero To work today with the new Turbo installed. It started bellowing white smoke out the exhaust on the way home. I have worked on this thing over the last 6 weeks, and I am now beyond my knowledge of what to do. Does anyone know of a professional garage that can work on a Turbo Fiero in the Roswell, GA area? I can deal with a good size area, but not another state. I need to get the car going because it is my daily driver to work, and has been sitting in the garage for the past month and a half. I need someone who knows what they are doing and can fix the car without having to keep it for another month to do it. Any help will be greatly appreciated. Thanks guys.||||reg||11
Z||000001||zeusrekning||12-18-2000||07:18 PM||||Do you know 1fst2m6?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||gixxer||12-18-2000||07:47 PM||||Is it from a kit, or did you piece it together?<BR>What brand of turbo?<BR>One thing that struck me as kind of odd reading thru turbo books is that some of them are sensitive to oil pressure, and that too much oil pressure (over 65#) may get oil thru the bearing seals. And then I presume, into the compressor or turbine area.<BR>I'm no turbo expert... Just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||12-18-2000||09:03 PM||||Get a hold of Ed at Engineered Performance in Smyrna.. they are just down the street from cumberland mall. Steve will answer the phone but he has this thing for not being helpful if you don't have a Nissan or a Honda. 770-434-0051 Let Ed know what your problem is and what actions you've taken so far. I'll call him at home right now and let him know your gunna be calling. Be sure and tell him travis told you to contact him. this car isn't your only means of transportation is it? i sure hope not... the shop pretty much closes up during the next week or so.. I'll be in minnesota on saturday returning on friday. <P>white smoke hunh.. do you have a rising rate fuel pressure regulator? or boost sensative ignition? how much boost are you running? how many miles are on the motor? have you checked the oil / coolant? have they mixed? do either look like chocolate milk? I'll check my mail again in the morning and get back with you shortly on what Ed says.. if you'd like i can get the phone # for the wrecker service we use and have them come get the car... bummer it failed so soon... manybe it'll be somthing easy to fix.<P>I got your e-mail... <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">   <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Predator||12-18-2000||09:12 PM||||Thanks for the quick response. IT's not my only driver but it is real inconvenient being without it. I will check all the things listed, and call Ed. Thanks again guys.||||reg||9
Z||000005||1FST2M6||12-18-2000||09:41 PM||||ok.. just spoke with Ed.. he's spent the last 6 hours dynoing a S/C Taurus SHO that was brought in from Texas. <P><BR>anywho.. ok He's gunna let Steve know not to blow you off in the morning. and to schedule a time/date that is good for you and the shop.. they are booked up and the shop is nearly full (only holds like 22 cars) not as many cars as you'd think. and ALL the customers cars sleep inside!  <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  he also said to check the plugs for fouling. and then check the intake for oil. if you blew a seal the intake will be full of oil (like a failing valve stem seal but worse) ||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||12-19-2000||08:48 PM||||I run 80 pnds oil pressure with no prob in 40,000 miles. My turbo only needs 4-5 pnds of boost for lots of power. How much were you trying? Kinda sounds to me (white smoke) that you blew one or both head gaskets. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Predator||12-19-2000||09:24 PM||||I never really got more than about 5 pounds of boost according to the guage. I wasn't kicking it. Just driving it down the expressway. The car only has 20,500 miles on it. I am going to find a shop in the area to take it to, and have the compression checked and hopefully to find out how bad it is. I need to find a good shop that can look at it. I can't wait weeks or months for it to get fixed. Thanks for the info guys. I figure it is a head gasket or worse. The car is in perfect shape and it just makes me sick to see it sitting there with possibly a blown engine, after all the time and money I have put into it. It would not bother me as much if I was doing something stupid with it, but this happening just driving normally down the road. After having the car appart for weeks this is very depressing to say the least. I am done trying to get it running myself, and I am going to just eat it, and pay the money for a professional to fix it right. I just have to find someone I can trust.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Predator||12-20-2000||08:07 AM||||Since it sounds like the garage will be closed for the holidays, and I too am very busy with the holidays I will probably wait until after the first of the year to call and get an appointmant to let them see my car 1FST2M6. I appreciate the help and direction. There is no oil and water mixture that I can find. I have AAA so I will probably use them to have the car towed there after I get the appointment made. Hopefully it won't be anything major, and they can check the Turbo out to make sure everything is setup correctly for me. I followed the directions with the kit, but it would be nice to have a professional look over the install and make sure this thing is correct. It has a knock sensor that I installed with it and I don't know how to test to make sure it is correct. To make a long story shorter it will be nice to have someone check the car over and make sure it is right. Thanks again. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||12-20-2000||08:27 AM||||ok.. cool.. AAA is FREE!! (well $50 a year ) but WAY cheaper than having Phoenix move it for ya.. Did you get a hold of Steve or Ed? were they helpful? where do you live? I can get the compression tester and leak down box from the shop and we can do that when i get back from MN. like saturday the 30th that'll save you a few bucks if you and I can diagnose it... maybe msweldon or Raydar might come and toss in their $.02. Plus i live next door to Ed so i can call him and ask for directions if we run into a problem.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> aaggh.. the joys of living next to an ASE MAster tech and fellow Ga. Tech grad..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Predator||12-20-2000||09:14 AM||||That sounds great. I appreciate the help. I am not much of an internal engine guy, and to be honest after all I did to get the Turbo kit installed, and now this happens I am a little gun shy on trying stuff myself. When it comes to diagnosing this kind of problem I don't know what I am doing. I would like to learn though. If you don't mind and have the time I would really appreciate you coming over and helping check the engine out. That would probably at least give me an idea of how bad it is, and what needs to be done. I really appreciate all your help. Email me when you can come over,a nd I will send you my phone number, and directions. ||||reg||7
